### Upload a blinker (3x3, horizontal phase). Returns 201 + Location.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "width": 3,
  "height": 3,
  "cells": [
    [false, false, false],
    [true,  true,  true ],
    [false, false, false]
  ]
}

### Board metadata and generation 0. Replace {id} with the id from above.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards/{id}

### F2: one generation forward. Call it twice -- the answer does not change.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards/{id}/next

### F3: ten generations away. A blinker at an even index matches generation 0.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards/{id}/generations/10

### F4: final state. A blinker reports CYCLE with period 2.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards/{id}/final

### F4 with an explicit limit.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards/{id}/final?maxGenerations=50

### F4 that gives up. A blinker needs two steps to see its cycle, so a limit of 1 is 422.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards/{id}/final?maxGenerations=1

### 400: maxGenerations must be at least 1.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards/{id}/final?maxGenerations=0

### 404 path.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/boards/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
